#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#. [set_menu_item]: id=sw_field_manual
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:271
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:287
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:282
msgid "Field Manual"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:288
msgid "Which section of the field manual?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:289
msgid "The Force and ysalamiri"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:289
msgid ""
"Jedi rely on the Force for <i>Force agility</i> (ignoring enemy zones of control), <i>Force healing</i> and <i>deflection</i> (turning blaster bolts back on the shooter).\n"
"\n"
"A ysalamiri pushes the Force back in a bubble around itself, shown as violet-tinted hexes. Inside that bubble every Force ability fails. Step out of it and the abilities return."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:292
msgid "Blaster fire"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:292
msgid ""
"The colour of a bolt tells you who is shooting: red for the Imperial Remnant and other dark forces, blue or green for the New Republic and its allies, orange for independent smugglers.\n"
"\n"
"Some craft keep their own colours: TIE starfighters and Star Destroyer turbolasers fire green, and X-wing, Y-wing and A-wing lasers fire red. Stun settings fire blue rings, and ion cannons fire a pale blue discharge that slows what it hits."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:295
msgid "Space battles"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:295
msgid ""
"Open space can only be crossed by starfighters and capital ships; ground troops stay aboard. Asteroid fields cost starfighters extra movement but give them cover, and capital ships cannot enter them.\n"
"\n"
"New squadrons launch from hangar bays and launch rails, which work like a keep and castle."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:298
msgid "Bases and settlements"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:298
msgid ""
"Command bunkers and shuttle landing pads are keeps: a leader standing on one can call in reinforcements onto the surrounding bunker aprons or landing aprons.\n"
"\n"
"Settlements, supply depots, Wookiee dwellings and Noghri dukhas count as villages: they heal units and earn credits each turn for whoever holds them. Bulkheads cannot be crossed."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:301
msgid "Heroes"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:301
msgid "Named heroes cannot be replaced. If one of the heroes named in a mission's objectives falls, the mission is lost. Heroes who survive continue to the next mission."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:302
msgid "Stealth and hidden hazards"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: utils/hte_macros.cfg:302
msgid ""
"Noghri commandos are invisible in forest or at night, unless an enemy with <i>keen senses</i> is within two hexes of them. They are revealed when an enemy moves next to them.\n"
"\n"
"Cloaked asteroids cannot be seen until something runs into them, and a ship that ends its turn next to one takes damage, though never enough to destroy it."
msgstr ""

